Objective
The objective of this lab was to identify and exploit misconfigured Linux capabilities to achieve privilege escalation. The focus was on discovering executables with elevated capabilities, leveraging them to access restricted files, and restoring user access by manipulating credentials.
Step 1: Enumerating Linux Capabilities
I began by enumerating the system to identify binaries with special Linux capabilities assigned.
During this process, I discovered:
Executables with elevated capabilities that allowed privileged actions
Misconfigured permissions enabling unintended access
This highlighted how improperly assigned capabilities can introduce privilege escalation vectors.
Step 2: Identifying a Vulnerable Executable
Next, I focused on a specific executable that had elevated privileges.
Through analysis, I was able to:
Identify how the binary could be abused
Leverage its capabilities to perform unauthorized actions
This demonstrated how attackers can exploit trusted binaries to bypass normal permission restrictions.
Step 3: Accessing Restricted User Files
Using the vulnerable executable, I was able to read sensitive files belonging to another user.
This allowed:
Access to protected user data
Extraction of information needed for further exploitation
This step showed how privilege escalation can lead to exposure of sensitive information.
Step 4: Restoring User Access
After gaining access to sensitive information, I used it to restore access to the user account.
This involved:
Resetting the user’s password
Regaining access to the system as that user
This demonstrated how attackers can manipulate credentials once sufficient privileges are obtained.
Step 5: Impact Analysis
Combining all findings, the system was vulnerable due to misconfigured Linux capabilities:
Improperly assigned capabilities to executables
Ability to access restricted files
Weak control over privileged operations
An attacker could leverage these issues to:
Escalate privileges beyond intended access
Read sensitive system and user data
Modify credentials and gain persistent access
Conclusion & Outcome
Through this lab, I gained hands-on experience exploiting Linux capabilities for privilege escalation. This exercise reinforced the importance of properly configuring capabilities and restricting access to sensitive binaries.
It also highlighted how small misconfigurations in privilege management can lead to full system compromise.
